---
import InsertLayout from '../layouts/InsertLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../utils/jsonld';

const jsonLd = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'About', url: '/about' }
]);
---

<InsertLayout
  title="About"
  description="Toledo Technologies is a remote software development studio. We build, fix, and ship code with transparency and precision. Learn about our approach and values."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  heading="About Toledo Technologies"
  subheading="A remote software development studio for builders who value craft over noise."
>
  <p>
    Toledo Technologies exists because too many development projects end in
    frustration. Scope creep. Poor communication. Code that works once but falls
    apart at scale. We built this studio to be the antidote.
  </p>

  <h2>The Short Version</h2>

  <p>
    We are a remote software development studio. We build, fix, and ship code
    for clients who need things done well—without the overhead of a full agency.
    Clear scoping upfront. Regular communication throughout. Clean code that
    gets handed off with documentation, not excuses.
  </p>

  <p>
    We work remotely, which means lower overhead and the ability to work with
    clients anywhere. It also means we've built the discipline to deliver
    without needing someone looking over our shoulder.
  </p>

  <h2>What We're Good At</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Fixing things that other developers broke (or that entropy broke)</li>
    <li>Building features and MVPs quickly without sacrificing quality</li>
    <li>Automating the tedious stuff so humans can focus on what matters</li>
    <li>Explaining technical decisions in plain language</li>
    <li>Handing off code that the next developer won't curse at</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How We Work</h2>

  <h3>Ship Clean</h3>
  <p>
    Code should work, be readable, and be maintainable. We don't cut corners
    that create future pain. Every line we write is written with the next
    developer in mind—even if that next developer is us, six months from now.
  </p>

  <h3>Communicate Clearly</h3>
  <p>
    No jargon walls. No disappearing acts. If there's a problem, you know
    immediately. We believe the most valuable thing we can give you is peace of
    mind, and that comes from knowing exactly where things stand.
  </p>

  <h3>Respect Constraints</h3>
  <p>
    Budget, timeline, technical debt—we work within reality, not against it. We
    won't promise what we can't deliver, and we won't pretend a two-week job can
    be done in two days.
  </p>

  <h3>Stay Curious</h3>
  <p>
    Technology moves fast. We stay current without chasing every shiny thing.
    The tools we recommend are the ones we've actually used, not the ones
    getting the most hype on social media.
  </p>

  <h2>Remote by Design</h2>

  <p>
    We don't have an office because we don't need one. Remote work lets us hire
    for talent (not geography), keep overhead low, and focus on what matters:
    shipping good code. Our clients span time zones. We're used to async
    communication, clear documentation, and working independently while staying
    connected.
  </p>

  <h2>See Our Work</h2>

  <p>
    Check out our public contributions and projects on GitHub. Production-ready
    code you can inspect before buying. 26+ repositories of sheer engineering.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a
      href="https://github.com/ntoledo319"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      github.com/ntoledo319 →
    </a>
  </p>

  <hr />

  <h2>Something broken? Something to build?</h2>

  <p>Tell us what you need. We'll tell you what it takes.</p>

  <p>
    <a href="/contact">Get a Quote →</a>
  </p>
</InsertLayout>
